[stderr] ## Red Flags
[stderr] 
[stderr] These thoughts mean STOP—you're rationalizing:
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Thought | Reality |
[stderr] |---------|---------|
[stderr] | "This is just a simple question" | Questions are tasks. Check for skills. |
[stderr] | "I need more context first" | Skill check comes BEFORE clarifying questions. |
[stderr] | "Let me explore the codebase first" | Skills tell you HOW to explore. Check first. |
[stderr] | "I can check git/files quickly" | Files lack conversation context. Check for skills. |
[stderr] | "Let me gather information first" | Skills tell you HOW to gather information. |
[stderr] | "This doesn't need a formal skill" | If a skill exists, use it. |
[stderr] | "I remember this skill" | Skills evolve. Read current version. |
[stderr] | "This doesn't count as a task" | Action = task. Check for skills. |
[stderr] | "The skill is overkill" | Simple things become complex. Use it. |
[stderr] | "I'll just do this one thing first" | Check BEFORE doing anything. |
[stderr] | "This feels productive" | Undisciplined action wastes time. Skills prevent this. |
[stderr] | "I know what that means" | Knowing the concept ≠ using the skill. Invoke it. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Skill Priority
[stderr] 
[stderr] When multiple skills could apply, use this order:
[stderr] 
[stderr] 1. **Process skills first** (brainstorming, debugging) - these determine HOW to approach the task
[stderr] 2. **Implementation skills second** (frontend-design, mcp-builder) - these guide execution
[stderr] 
[stderr] "Let's build X" → brainstorming first, then implementation skills.
[stderr] "Fix this bug" → debugging first, then domain-specific skills.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Skill Types
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Rigid** (TDD, debugging): Follow exactly. Don't adapt away discipline.
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Flexible** (patterns): Adapt principles to context.
[stderr] 
[stderr] The skill itself tells you which.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## User Instructions
[stderr] 
[stderr] Instructions say WHAT, not HOW. "Add X" or "Fix Y" doesn't mean skip workflows.
